# Local state of the template app when it is run in place during development.
# npm applies this file because it lives in a subdirectory listed in the root "files" field.
#
# During development the template app is its own git repository (npm run template:setup) with
# the document-templates submodule. The generated project gets its own, created by the CLI, so
# none of that may be published inside the package. npm drops .git itself.
.gitmodules
document-templates/
node_modules/
.next/
out/
.env
.env.local
next-env.d.ts
package-lock.json
pnpm-lock.yaml
yarn.lock
bun.lockb
bun.lock
*.tsbuildinfo
storage/*
!storage/.gitkeep
AGENTS.md
